    "title": "What we learned about what makes up Avon Lake's $48 million road estimate - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Michael Johnson, cleveland.com cleveland.com Express Desk ,\n1 days ago AVON LAKE, Ohio — Avon Lake’s estimated $48 million in road needs is not limited to rebuilding streets already in poor condition. About $24 million is tied to roads the city rates poor or failed. The other $24 million represents preventive maintenance for streets still rated fair, good or excellent — work intended to keep them from deteriorating into more expensive repair categories. Read full article",
